{
  "editions": [
    {
      "edition": "standard",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": true,
        "no_added_claims": false,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "speaker_attribution": true,
        "source_choices_and_notes": false,
        "terminology_policy": true
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "[τὸν ποιμένα]",
          "english_quote": "After the shepherd had examined everyone’s rods, he said to me",
          "issue": "The translation incorporates the bracketed identification of the shepherd without disclosing that it is an editorial supplement. The supplied source warnings explicitly distinguish brackets from preserved manuscript words. The same disclosure problem applies to the final bracketed speaker tag, [φησίν], rendered as “he said.”",
          "suggested_revision": "Add a reader-facing note identifying the opening shepherd identification and the final “he said” as editorial supplements in the selected working Greek, rather than preserved manuscript wording. They need not be removed from the translation.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "καὶ ἐγένετο ἡ κατοικία αὐτῶν εἰς τὰ τείχη τὰ πρῶτα",
          "english_quote": "and their dwelling came to be in the outer walls",
          "issue": "“Outer” replaces the source’s ordinal “first” with a spatial identification not established by this selected passage. The note acknowledges “the first walls” but does not provide evidence that these are specifically outer walls. Distinction from the tower alone does not establish that identification.",
          "suggested_revision": "Use “and their dwelling came to be in the first walls,” or supply contextual evidence establishing that “outer” faithfully represents the ordinal here. Any replacement requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "major"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ἡ μετάνοια τῶν ἁμαρτωλῶν",
          "english_quote": "μετάνοια / διψυχεῖν",
          "issue": "The lexical metadata lists διψυχεῖν and a chosen rendering “waver,” although that verb does not occur anywhere in the selected source. This falsely presents an out-of-unit lexical decision as a decision for this passage.",
          "suggested_revision": "Remove the διψυχεῖν / “waver” material from this unit’s lexical decision, or explicitly identify it as cross-unit metadata rather than a source expression translated here.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": "simplified",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": false,
        "no_added_claims": false,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "speaker_attribution": true,
        "source_choices_and_notes": false,
        "terminology_policy": true
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "[τὸν ποιμένα]",
          "english_quote": "The shepherd examined everyone’s rods.",
          "issue": "The shepherd identification is incorporated without disclosing that the selected Greek supplies it editorially in brackets. Its contextual plausibility does not make it preserved manuscript wording.",
          "suggested_revision": "Add a reader-facing note identifying “the shepherd” in the opening sentence as an editorial supplement in the selected working Greek.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "νῦν οὖν μοι δήλωσον τοὺς τὰς ῥάβδους ἐπιδεδωκότας, ποταπός τις αὐτῶν ἐστι, καὶ τὴν τούτων κατοικίαν, ἵνα ἀκούσαντες οἱ πιστεύσαντες καὶ εἰληφότες τὴν σφραγῖδα καὶ τεθλακότες αὐτὴν καὶ μὴ τηρήσαντες ὑγιῆ, ἐπιγνόντες τὰ ἑαυτῶν ἔργα μετανοήσωσι",
          "english_quote": "Sir, explain what sort of people handed in the rods and where they dwell. Some people believed and received the seal, but broke it and did not keep it sound. Let them hear, recognize their own deeds and repent",
          "issue": "The source makes hearing, recognizing their deeds, and repenting the purpose of the requested explanation. The simplified text replaces that connection with a separate factual statement and an independent “Let them” exhortation. It also omits the explicit “now, then” transition.",
          "suggested_revision": "Preserve the purpose connection, for example: “Sir, now explain what sort of people handed in the rods and where they dwell, so that those who believed and received the seal, but broke it and did not keep it sound, may hear, recognize their own deeds, and repent.” Review the continuation with the renewed seal together with this proposed wording.",
          "severity": "major"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "καὶ ἐγένετο ἡ κατοικία αὐτῶν εἰς τὰ τείχη τὰ πρῶτα",
          "english_quote": "Their dwelling was in the outer walls.",
          "issue": "“Outer” substitutes an unsupported spatial identification for “first.” In addition, “was” drops the source’s result or change expressed by ἐγένετο: their dwelling came to be there following the preceding account of repentance and becoming good.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider “Their dwelling came to be in the first walls.” A simpler alternative must retain both the ordinal and the resulting placement; review the proposed replacement before acceptance.",
          "severity": "major"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "βλέπεις δὲ πολλοὺς ἐξ αὐτῶν καὶ μετανενοηκότας ἀφ᾿ ἧς ἐλάλησας αὐτοῖς τὰς ἐντολάς μου",
          "english_quote": "Many have repented since you spoke my commandments to them.",
          "issue": "The explicit “of them” is omitted. This identifies the repentant people as members of the preceding hypocritical-teacher group, an important qualification after that group is said to have hope of repentance. The simplified wording leaves “many” less specifically identified.",
          "suggested_revision": "Restore the group link, for example: “You see that many of them have repented since you spoke my commandments to them.”",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ἡ μετάνοια τῶν ἁμαρτωλῶν",
          "english_quote": "μετάνοια / διψυχεῖν",
          "issue": "The simplified edition independently repeats lexical metadata for διψυχεῖν / “waver,” although that expression is absent from the selected Greek. The metadata therefore attributes a lexical decision to this unit that its source does not support.",
          "suggested_revision": "Remove the absent verb and its rendering from this unit’s lexical metadata, or clearly label them as cross-unit information.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Both editions require revision. They retain the difficult repentance assertions, negations, renewed seal, plural spirits, and policy-compliant servant terminology. The disclosed bounded “sinners” selection agrees with the supplied project report, including the partial Michigan restoration and the differing historical 1891 noun; it should not be replaced merely because that alternative exists. The main defects are undisclosed editorial supplementation, unsupported “outer walls,” stray lexical metadata, and additional losses in the simplified edition. This review assesses the supplied working source and reports, not unseen manuscripts or an exhaustive collation. Proposed corrections remain subject to fresh review."
}
